{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Wave_of_the_Hand","to":"Wave of the Hand"},{"from":"Panic_Button","to":"Panic Button"},{"from":"Cut_Through_Fate","to":"Cut Through Fate"},{"from":"Sadistic_Nature","to":"Sadistic Nature"},{"from":"Tools_of_the_Trade","to":"Tools of the Trade"},{"from":"Ball_Lightning","to":"Ball Lightning"},{"from":"Heel_Hook","to":"Heel Hook"},{"from":"Die_Die_Die","to":"Die Die Die"}],"pages":{"2058":{"pageid":2058,"ns":0,"title":"Ball Lightning","revisions":[{"revid":56891,"parentid":55634,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation|1|1}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Ball Lightning\n|Image       = Blue-BallLightning.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage. {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Lightning}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Lightning, Channel\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}\n{{C|Ball Lightning}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.<!---It deals 7 (10) damage, then {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning}} Orbs less effective.\n\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Ball Lightning+ card nerf: Upgrade damage 4 -> 3.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2460":{"pageid":2460,"ns":0,"title":"Bite","revisions":[{"revid":55649,"parentid":50756,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bite\n|Image       = Colorless-Bite.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;8) damage.<br>Heal (2;3) HP.\n}}\n{{C|Bite}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (8 if upgrade) damage and heals you for 2 (3 if upgraded) HP.\n\n== Obtaining Bite ==\n{{C|Bite}} is an [[Events]]-only card, and the only way to obtain it is through the event {{E|Vampires}}, which will give 5 copies of {{C|Bite}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nThe healing from {{C|Bite}} takes effect after receiving damage from {{BD|Thorns}} or {{BD|Sharp Hide}}, but before taking damage with {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} increases the effectiveness of the healing.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Healing cards cannot be generated mid-combat to avoid infinite healing, so {{C|Bite}} cannot be created by something like {{C|Infernal Blade}}, {{C|Metamorphosis}} or {{R|Dead Branch}}. \n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Bonfire Spirits event now correctly handles offering them a card with the Special rarity (like Bite, or Apparition).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating SFX for Vampire Bite.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Bite SFX now plays a different SFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Bite now correctly works when last hitting in fast mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Rewards after combat appear only when all actions are done now. Fast Mode + Bite bug fix.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Bite is now a Colorless card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Bites now correctly get marked as seen in the card library when obtained.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Adding Bite VFX to Bite cards.\n** Fix for Bite cards not loading correctly (it gave you Madness cards) when resuming a run.\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1869":{"pageid":1869,"ns":0,"title":"Blasphemy","revisions":[{"revid":56898,"parentid":56409,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Blasphemy\n| Image       = Purple-Blasphemy.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = (;{{KW|Retain}}.<br>)Enter {{KW|Divinity}}.<br>Die next turn.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Divinity, Blasphemer, Retain\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Blasphemer}}{{C|Blasphemy}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. When played, the card exhausts and causes Watcher to enter {{KW|Divinity|Divinity}}, which grants 3 {{Icon|PE}} Energy and triples the damage of your attacks for the rest of the turn. The price of this effect is that the Watcher becomes a {{BD|Blasphemer}}, ensuring 99999 self damage next turn. When upgraded, the card {{KW|Retain|Retains}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{KW|Retain|Retaining}} attacks in hand such as {{C|Windmill Strike}} ensures you will have ammo for when {{C|Blasphemy}} is used.\n\n* {{BD|Vulnerable}} scales multiplicatively with {{KW|Divinity}} for a massive total 4.5x damage multiplier.\n\n* {{C|Blasphemy}} generates a lot of energy, which greatly benefits from card draw.\n\n* {{R|Lizard Tail}} and {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}} allows you to survive {{BD|Blasphemer}}.\n\n* As the upgraded version of {{C|Blasphemy}} {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n==== Negating Blasphemer ====\nDespite the card text of {{C|Blasphemy}} outright telling that it kills Watcher, it actually deals 99999 HP loss, which can be prevented.\n\n* {{R|Fossilized Helix}} completely blocks {{BD|Blasphemer}}.\n\n* {{BD|Intangible}} reduces {{BD|Blasphemer}} damage to 1. However, since {{BD|Intangible}} counts down at the beginning of your turn, you need at least 2 stacks to protect yourself.\n** {{R|Incense Burner}} gives {{BD|Intangible}} at the beginning of your turn, so it can protect you even though it grants only 1 stack. Make sure its counter is on 5 the turn you play {{C|Blasphemy}}.\n** Since {{BD|Blasphemer}} is HP loss, the 1 cannot be blocked by regular {{KW|Block}} cards.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Blasphemy}} does not generate {{BD|Mantra}}, so it does not scale up the damage of {{C|Brilliance}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Blasphemer}} is intentionally treated as a \"[[Buffs|positive buff]]\" by the game, and thus cannot be blocked by {{BD|Artifact}} or removed with {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n\n* Cards that change your {{KW|Stance}} will remove {{KW|Divinity}} without removing the {{BD|Blasphemer}} effect.\n\n* {{C|Conclude}}, {{C|Meditate}}, {{C|Vault}} and {{BD|Time Warp}} forcibly end your turn, likely resulting in your death.\n\n* Effects that play cards from your draw pile for free (like {{C|Mayhem}} and {{P|Distilled Chaos}}) may end up playing {{C|Blasphemy}} before you are ready.\n\n* {{BD|Invincible}} and {{BD|Unawakened}} may prevent you from ending the combat in one turn.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Max HP is not capped in Slay the Spire, which means it's possible (but unfeasible) to increase your HP so high you can survive {{BD|Blasphemer}}.\n** One way this could be done is using 2 {{C|Nightmare|Nightmares}} to generate a large number of {{C|Nightmare|Nightmares}}, then using these cards to {{C|Wish}} for a massive quantity of [[Gold]], which can be used with {{R|The Courier}} to buy an endless amount of {{P|Fruit Juice}} at the [[Merchant]].\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2206":{"pageid":2206,"ns":0,"title":"Buffer","revisions":[{"revid":56916,"parentid":55191,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Buffer\n|Image       = Blue-Buffer.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Prevent the next (time;2 times) you would lose HP.\n|GivesToPlayer = Buffer\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Buffer\n|Image        = Icon Buffer.png\n|Description  = Prevent the next X times you would lose HP.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Counter\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Lose HP\n}}\n{{C|Buffer}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Buffer}}, preventing the next instance(s) of losing HP.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Fixed Self-Forming Clay relic triggering incorrectly off of prevented damage from Buffer power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Painful Stabs power will no longer give wounds if the damage was prevented by Buffer.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Effects that trigger on damage like Masterful Stab now interacts properly with damage prevention effects like Buffer.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Buffer is no longer lost when hit by 0 damage attacks.\n** Centennial Puzzle no longer draws cards when taking 0 damage as a result of things like Buffer.\n** Shelled Parasite now accounts for Buffer and Intangible with its life leech action.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2118":{"pageid":2118,"ns":0,"title":"Bullseye","revisions":[{"revid":56920,"parentid":55673,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bullseye\n|Image       = Blue-Bullseye.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;11) damage.<br>Apply (2;3) {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Lock-On\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Lock-On\n|Image        = Icon LockOn.png\n|Description  = Receives 50% more damage from {{KW|Orb|Orbs}} for X turns.\n|Type         = Debuff\n|Stacks       = Duration\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Orb\n}}\n{{C|Bullseye}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* In general, additive effects are applied before multiplicative ones. If a damaging Orb is improved by {{BD|Focus}} and then damages an enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}, the {{BD|Focus}} will be added before the 50% increase from {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Lock-On}} improves the damage of all {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Dark}} Orb sources.\n* {{C|Electrodynamics}} is helpful in multi enemy combats for making sure the damage from {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hits the enemy with {{BD|Lock-On}}.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} apply before {{BD|Lock-On}}, allowing for large damage output: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}.\n* In addition to general Orb sources, cards that can manually {{KW|Evoke}} Orbs can be very useful for dealing damage with {{BD|Lock-On}}: {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, {{C|Multi-Cast}}\n** {{C|Fission}} is a particular powerful option for this, allowing all of your damaging Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} while the [[Debuff]] is active.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, reducing the damage output of your Orbs.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Bullseye is the only source in the game of {{BD|Lock-On}}. It is not unique in this regard, as {{BD|Mark}} has {{C|Pressure Points}} as its only source.\n* The art of Bullseye appears to be a {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Dark}} Orb being fired at [[Donu]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Bullseye card buffed. Lock-On 1 -> 2.\n** Bullseye+ card buffed. Damage 10 -> 11.\n\n* '''Switch Version 1.02'''\n** Fixed Lock-On bug\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Lock-On Power no longer incorrectly has the focused targeting effect.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Lock-On card reworked.\n** Lock-On card renamed -> Bullseye.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1906":{"pageid":1906,"ns":0,"title":"Corruption","revisions":[{"revid":56614,"parentid":56433,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Corruption\n| Image       = Red-Corruption.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 3\n| CostPlus    = 2\n| Description = Skills cost 0.<br>Whenever you play a Skill, {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n| PowerGives = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Corruption\n| Image        = Icon Corruption.png\n| Description  = {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} cost 0. Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Does not stack\n| BetweenTurns = \n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Corruption}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Corruption}}, which makes all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} have an {{Icon|RE}}-cost of 0, and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} them after they are played. As {{BD|Corruption}} does not stack, copies of {{C|Corruption}} played after the first have no additional effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}}, most notably {{C|Dark Embrace}}, as it allows you to keep drawing new {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}}, and {{R|Dead Branch}}, as it allows you to keep playing any {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} you draw or create. \n\n=== Neutral ===\n* With {{BD|Corruption}}, when randomizing the '''Energy''' {{Icon|RE}}-cost of cards through {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}}, the cost of all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards will remain 0.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** (Undocumented) Rarity changed from Uncommon to Rare.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Confusion and Corruption cards utilize improved hooks.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2284":{"pageid":2284,"ns":0,"title":"Cut Through Fate","revisions":[{"revid":56955,"parentid":50639,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Cut Through Fate\n|Image       = Purple-CutThroughFate.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;9) damage. <br>{{KW|Scry}} (2;3). <br>Draw 1 card.\n|GivesToPlayer = Draw, Scry\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Scry}}\n{{C|Cut Through Fate}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (9 if upgraded) damage. It allows you to {{KW|Scry}} 2 (3 if upgraded) and then draw 1 card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Cut Through Fate}} allows you to {{KW|Scry}} before drawing the card, meaning you can effectively choose which of the shown cards, if any, are drawn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have {{R|Golden Eye}}, you will be able to {{KW|Scry}} 2 more cards.\n* Playing {{C|Cut Through Fate}} will activate {{C|Nirvana}}.\n* As it allows you to {{KW|Scry}}, any {{C|Weave}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand. \n** If a {{C|Weave}} is among the cards {{KW|Scry|Scryed}} by {{C|Cut Through Fate}} and is discarded this way, it will immediately be brought back into your hand.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2018":{"pageid":2018,"ns":0,"title":"Deflect","revisions":[{"revid":56793,"parentid":50480,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Deflect\n| Image       = Green-Deflect.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Gain (4;7) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Deflect}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 4 (7 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Deflect+ card buff: 6 -> 7 Block.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2036":{"pageid":2036,"ns":0,"title":"Die Die Die","revisions":[{"revid":55742,"parentid":50533,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Die Die Die\n|Image       = Green-DieDieDie.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (13;17) damage to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Die Die Die}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 13 (17 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} when played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card is a reference to Overwatch, particularly the character Reaper having the same name as his ultimate and art of Silent striking a similar pose Reaper often has.\n* The beta design of this card shows 3 dice, which is an obvious pun.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Buff: Now {{KW|Exhaust}}s instead of subtracting 2 {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"2288":{"pageid":2288,"ns":0,"title":"Evaluate","revisions":[{"revid":55767,"parentid":54828,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Evaluate\n|Image       = Purple-Evaluate.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (6;10) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Shuffle an {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile.\n}} \n{{Small Card Infobox|Insight}}\n{{C|Evaluate}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 6 (10 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and shuffles 1 {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order === \n* The {{C|Insight}} gets added into your draw pile before triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will shuffle an upgraded {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile instead.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Insight}} has no effect on its own except for cycling through cards, it is not benefitial when there is a restriction or downside to playing ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}) cards, such as with {{BD|Time Warp}}, {{BD|Hex}}, {{BD|Beat of Death}} or {{R|Velvet Choker}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2461":{"pageid":2461,"ns":0,"title":"Expunger","revisions":[{"revid":53293,"parentid":50757,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"#REDIRECT [[Conjure Blade#Expunger]]"}}}]},"2054":{"pageid":2054,"ns":0,"title":"Heel Hook","revisions":[{"revid":55817,"parentid":55441,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Heel Hook\n|Image       = Green-HeelHook.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (5;8) damage. <br>If the enemy has {{BD|Weak}}, <br>gain {{Icon|GE}} and draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Energy\n}}\n{{C|Heel Hook}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (8 if upgraded) damage. If the target has {{BD|Weak}}, gain 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' and draw 1 card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* No matter what {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{C|Heel Hook}} has, the player will always gain 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if it is played on a target with {{BD|Weak}}. This can be used to your advantage by reducing the cost below 1, but can lose you {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' as well if the cost is increased:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Setup}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain, although this extra energy is often useless.\n* {{C|Madness}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* If {{C|Heel Hook}} is selected from an {{P|Attack Potion}} it will have a cost of 0, resulting in 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{BD|Confused}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}} will randomize the cost from 0 to 3, which can result in a neutral, gained or lost amount of energy.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Heel Hook card now resolves its actions in order of its description.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Heel Hook+ card buffed. 7 -> 8 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Fixed rare crash for HeelHook card.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1929":{"pageid":1929,"ns":0,"title":"Hemokinesis","revisions":[{"revid":50431,"parentid":35958,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Hemokinesis\n|Image       = Red-Hemokinesis.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Lose 2 HP.<br>Deal (15;20) damage.\n}}\n{{C|Hemokinesis}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It costs 2 HP to play, and deals 15 (20 if upgraded) damage. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Hemokinesis}} can be used to trigger {{C|Rupture}}, {{R|Runic Cube}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}, and control the activation of {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Hemokinesis card buffed. Damage increased from 14 -> 15.\n** Hemokinesis card buffed. HP loss decreased from 3 -> 2.\n** Hemokinesis+ card buffed. Damage increased from 18 -> 20.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 55: Blur'''\n** Adding VFX for Hemokinesis card.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2270":{"pageid":2270,"ns":0,"title":"Indignation","revisions":[{"revid":55822,"parentid":54869,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Indignation\n|Image       = Purple-Indignation.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = If you are in {{KW|Wrath}}, apply (3;5) {{BD|Vulnerable}} to ALL enemies,<br>otherwise enter {{KW|Wrath}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Wrath}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{C|Indignation}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. If you are in the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}}, it applies 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}} to '''ALL''' enemies. If you were not in {{KW|Wrath}} when playing this card, it makes you enter {{KW|Wrath}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Wrath}} if you are not in {{KW|Wrath}} yet:\n** If you have {{BD|Rushdown}} from {{C|Rushdown}}, you will draw that many cards.\n** You will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n*** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n*** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n*** If you were in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} before, you will gain 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''', or 3 if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Wrath}} changes the effects of some cards:\n** {{C|Halt}} will give its additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** Playing a successive {{C|Indignation}} will apply {{BD|Vulnerable}}, meaning this card synergizes with itself, and will have a different effect if played twice, either normally or through effects such as {{C|Omniscience}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While in {{KW|Wrath}}, all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage you deal is doubled, but you also take double damage from enemy attacks.{{KW|Wrath}} only doubles damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, not from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{KW|Wrath}} is worse than the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}} in every way except for the aformentioned ones, using {{C|Indignation}} while in {{KW|Divinity}} is generally bad.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2475":{"pageid":2475,"ns":0,"title":"Panic Button","revisions":[{"revid":55886,"parentid":50735,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Panic Button\n|Image       = Colorless-PanicButton.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (30;40) {{KW|Block}}. You cannot gain {{KW|Block}} from cards for 2 turns.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Power Infobox|No Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Panic Button}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 30 (40 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and 2 {{BD|No Block}}, which prevents you from gaining {{KW|Block}} from cards for that amount of turns. It then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Panic Button ==\n{{C|Panic Button}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|No Block}} only puts the value of {{KW|Block}} on a card to 0, which means that:\n** {{C|Entrench}} can still double your {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Wallop}} can still give you {{KW|Block}} equal to unblocked damage dealt.\n** {{KW|Block}} gained from other sources if unaffected, meaning relics such as {{R|Orichalcum}}, potions such as {{P|Block Potion}}, and [[Buffs]] such as {{BD|After Image}} or {{BD|Next Turn Block}} from {{C|Dodge and Roll}} function as normal. {{KW|Frost}} also functions as normal.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for No Block power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Panic Button.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1820":{"pageid":1820,"ns":0,"title":"Sadistic Nature","revisions":[{"revid":55930,"parentid":50747,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sadistic Nature\n|Image       = Colorless-SadisticNature.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Whenever you apply a debuff to an enemy, they take (5;7) damage.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Sadistic}}\n{{C|Sadistic Nature}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It applies the {{BD|Sadistic}} effect on the player, allowing you to deal 5 (7) damage to any enemy they apply a [[Debuff]] to.\n\n== Obtaining Sadistic Nature ==\n{{C|Sadistic Nature}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n{{BD|Sadistic}} deals damage each time a [[Debuff]] is applied to an enemy.\n* If a single source applies multiple debuffs (for example {{C|Uppercut}}), each unique debuff will trigger {{BD|Sadistic}} once.\n* If a single source applies a debuff multiple times (for example {{C|Bouncing Flask}}), {{BD|Sadistic}} will trigger each time.\n\n==== Ironclad ====\n* Triggers {{BD|Sadistic}} multiple times: {{C|Uppercut}}, {{C|Shockwave}}\n* {{C|Bash}}, {{C|Clothesline}}, {{C|Thunderclap}}, {{C|Disarm}}, {{C|Intimidate}}\n* {{R|Champion Belt}}\n\n==== Silent ====\n* Triggers {{BD|Sadistic}} multiple times: {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}, {{C|Envenom}}, {{C|Malaise}}\n* {{C|Neutralize}}, {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Piercing Wail}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Sucker Punch}}, {{C|Catalyst}}, {{C|Choke}}, {{C|Leg Sweep}}, {{C|Terror}}\n* {{R|The Specimen}}\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}\n\n==== Defect ====\n* {{C|Beam Cell}}, {{C|Go for the Eyes}}, {{C|Bullseye}}\n\n==== Watcher ====\n* Triggers {{BD|Sadistic}} multiple times: {{C|Wave of the Hand}}\n* {{C|Crush Joints}}, {{C|Pressure Points}}, {{C|Sash Whip}}, {{C|Indignation}}, {{C|Talk to the Hand}}\n\n==== All characters ====\n* {{C|Blind}}, {{C|Dark Shackles}}, {{C|Trip}}\n* {{R|Hand Drill}}\n* {{P|Fear Potion}}, {{P|Weak Potion}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n==== Snecko Skull ====\nAlthough {{R|Snecko Skull}} increases the amount of {{BD|Poison}} applied, it does not activate Sadistic an extra time.\n\n==== Strength ====\nIs completely unaffected by {{BD|Strength}}. This means the debuff from {{M|Spire Shield|Spire Shield's}} {{Int|Spire Shield|Bash}} will have no effect on it, but neither will {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Vajra}}, or {{C|Inflame}}.\n\n==== Thorns and Flight ====\nAs Sadistic Nature does not do Attack damage, it bypasses {{M|Spiker|Spikers'}} {{BD|Thorns}} and {{M|Byrd|Byrds'}} {{BD|Flying}}, but it also does not benefit from {{M|Giant Head|Giant Head's}} {{BD|Slow}}.\n\n==== Stances ====\nSimilarly, the damage from Sadistic Nature is not affected by being in [[Wrath]] or [[Divinity]].\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2261":{"pageid":2261,"ns":0,"title":"Scrape","revisions":[{"revid":55491,"parentid":50603,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Scrape\n|Image       = Blue-Scrape.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (7;10) damage.<br>Draw (4;5) cards.<br>Discard all cards drawn this way that do not cost 0.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Discard\n}}\n{{C|Scrape}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage, and will draw 4 (5 if upgraded) cards. It will discard all cards drawn by it that do not cost 0. 0 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' does not have to be the base {{Icon|BE}}-cost of that card, as long as it costs 0 upon being drawn by {{C|Scrape}}, it will not be discarded.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* It synergizes with every {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue&cost:0|0-cost card}}, all of which that belong to the Defect listed below:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Beam Cell}}, {{C|Claw}}, {{C|Go for the Eyes}}, {{C|Steam Barrier}}, {{C|TURBO}}, {{C|FTL}}, and {{C|Overclock}}. \n* If not yet {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by playing them, {{C|Boot Sequence}}, {{C|Chill}}, {{C|Fission}}, {{C|Reboot}}, and {{C|Seek}}.\n* If upgraded, {{C|Dualcast}}, {{C|Zap}}, and {{C|Recycle}}.  \n* If upgraded and not yet {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by playing them, {{C|Double Energy}} and {{C|White Noise}}\n* {{C|Streamline}} and {{C|Force Field}}, as long as they have been reduced to 0 cost already.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Cards with no concrete {{Icon|BE}}-cost, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}}, and X-cost cards will always be discarded by {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* It competes for functionality with {{C|All for One}}, as both synergize well with 0-cost cards. The chance that {{C|Scrape}} can draw and discard {{C|All for One}} means that these two cards actually do not synergize, contrary to expectations.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Scrape card draws 3 -> 4 cards.\n** Scrape+ card buffed. Damage increased from 9 -> 10.\n** Scrape+ card draws 4 -> 5 cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Scrape card gets VFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Scrape and All For One cards now correctly work with cards that set cost to 0 until played.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2030":{"pageid":2030,"ns":0,"title":"Tools of the Trade","revisions":[{"revid":55981,"parentid":55515,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Tools of the Trade\n|Image       = Green-ToolsoftheTrade.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 1\n|CostPlus    = 0\n|Description = At the start of your turn, draw 1 card and discard 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Discard\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Tools Of The Trade}}{{C|Tools of the Trade}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Tools Of The Trade}}, which draws 1 card and makes you select 1 card to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] at the start of every turn.\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Tools of the Trade}}'s repeated [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics: \n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by 1 {{Icon|GE}} Energy every turn.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} Energy every turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} Energy every turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Tools of the Trade}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Tools of the Trade power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Tools of the Trade card nerf. No longer innate.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2407":{"pageid":2407,"ns":0,"title":"Wallop","revisions":[{"revid":55997,"parentid":54866,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wallop\n|Image       = Purple-Wallop.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (9;12) damage.<br>Gain {{KW|Block}} equal to unblocked damage dealt.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Wallop}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (12 if upgraded) damage, and gives {{KW|Block}} equal to the amount of unblocked damage it dealt. You will only gain {{KW|Block}} equal to the amount of HP actually lost by the enemy, so killing an enemy with damage remaining will only give you {{KW|Block}} equal to the HP they had left. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Wallop}} gives {{KW|Block}} before taking any damage from {{BD|Thorns}} or {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Any increase to the damage output of {{C|Wallop}} will also boost its {{KW|Block}}:\n** {{BD|Vulnerable}} on the target.\n** Any positive amount of {{BD|Strength}}. \n** {{BD|Vigor}}.\n** Being in the {{KW|Wrath}} or {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* As the {{KW|Block}} is fully dependent on the damage dealt by this card, it is unaffected by {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|Frail}}, but since the {{KW|Block}} still originates from a card, {{BD|No Block}} from {{C|Panic Button}} still applies.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2408":{"pageid":2408,"ns":0,"title":"Wave of the Hand","revisions":[{"revid":55998,"parentid":50687,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wave of the Hand\n|Image       = Purple-WaveoftheHand.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you gain {{KW|Block}} this turn, apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}} to ALL enemies.\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Wave of the Hand}}\n{{C|Wave of the Hand}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Wave of the Hand}}, which applies that amount of {{BD|Weak}} to '''ALL''' enemies whenever you gain {{KW|Block}} in any way.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]}}}}